Z||000011||AusFiero||07-18-2001||12:31 PM||||Beleive it or not them Jags cost about half of what a Fiero does in Australia. There is some really hot ones around with the V8 conversions available. We can buy XJS's for about $2500 and the XJE above a good one with Chev engine and work on it is less than $10K. A V12 one, can hardly give them away. I must be mad driving a Fiero huh  <IMG SRC="http://www.fiero.nl/forum/smile.gif"><P>Hey Bill, I do a little flying too. Not licensed yet but that is my next goal. Have been on many a flight where I just get given the controls, I can take off and fly, haven't landed the thing yet.<P>I have some Aussie aircraft Memoribillia you may well be interested in trading something USA for.<P><P>------------------<BR>   <IMG SRC="http://www.jadeweb.com.au/fiero/fiero5.gif">   <BR><A HREF="http://www.jadeweb.com.au/fiero" TARGET=_blank>My Fiero</A><BR>Need a Subwoofer Console or Speaker Door Pods?||||reg||1
Z||000012||84Bill||07-18-2001||12:58 PM||||Cool Aus!! I Soloed on Christmas day 1999 it was the best Christmas present ever I got. Nothing like being all alone in the wild blue  <IMG SRC="http://www.fiero.nl/forum/wink.gif"> I have 23 hours and stopped because of money but I will soon get back in the air and finish up. The plane (Grumman AA1B) I learned in was alot like the Fiero in many ways bastardized and beaten by many but a really fun plane to fly  <IMG SRC="http://www.fiero.nl/forum/biggrin.gif">||||reg||14
